  <h2>Flare leggings, bootcut yoga pants and wide-leg pants are not identical</h2>
  <p>A product photo can make these shapes look similar. Flare leggings normally stay fitted through the hip and upper leg, then open below the knee. Bootcut often suggests a smaller opening. Wide-leg pants carry more width through the thigh. Retail terminology is inconsistent, so a wholesale order should name measurable points: waist, hip, thigh, knee, leg opening and inseam. A reference image helps, but it should support the specification rather than replace it.</p>
  <p>Compare actual Fitclo examples. <a href="/products/tz2557-6/">TZ2557-6</a> combines a seamless halter tank with high-waist flare leggings. <a href="/products/tz4506-3/">TZ4506-3</a> pairs a halter top with contrast-trim flare pants. Their visual details differ; confirm each product's fabric, sizes, colors and current stock before choosing one for your range. For broader options, browse <a href="/products/matching-sets/">matching activewear sets</a>.</p>

  <h2>Specify the fit with a measurement table</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Measurement</th><th>Why the buyer needs it</th><th>Sample check</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Rise and waist</td><td>Sets waistband position and coverage</td><td>Check rolling, sliding and comfort during bending</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Hip and thigh</td><td>Controls fit through the upper leg</td><td>Assess drag lines, stretch and opacity on different bodies</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Knee width</td><td>Shows where the flare begins</td><td>Compare the worn silhouette with the approved reference</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Leg opening</td><td>Defines how wide the hem looks</td><td>Check symmetry and whether the hem overwhelms the intended look</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Inseam</td><td>Determines where the hem falls</td><td>Record the sample size, wearer height and footwear used for approval</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>Use a base size and tolerance for each point, then review grading into the other sizes. An inseam that works on one model may pool at the floor or look short on another. Ask the supplier how the hem and leg opening change across the size run. The <a href="/blogs/activewear-sizing-and-grading-guide/">activewear sizing and grading guide</a> explains how to make these decisions before bulk production.</p>

  <h2>Fabric recovery matters as much as softness</h2>
  <p>A soft hand feel is useful, but it does not tell you whether the knees bag out after repeated movement or whether a waistband stays in place. Review a sample after wear and washing, and write down what level of change is acceptable. <a href="https://store.astm.org/d2594_d2594m-21.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ASTM D2594/D2594M</a> describes a method for measuring stretch and fabric growth in certain knits and explains why recovery matters for form-fitting apparel. The appropriate laboratory method depends on the actual fabric and performance requirement; ask a qualified lab to confirm it.</p>
  <p>For lighter colors, check opacity while the garment is stretched. For contrast trims or dark-on-light panels, decide whether colorfastness testing is needed for washing, perspiration and rubbing. See our <a href="/blogs/activewear-colorfastness-testing-guide/">colorfastness buyer guide</a> for the test brief. If the product is sold as a set, evaluate the top and bottom together for shade, fit and care behavior.</p>

  <h2>Ready-stock or private label: ask for an exact quote</h2>
  <p>The linked TZ2557-6 and TZ4506-3 pages list 50 sets as a ready-stock MOQ. That number is a useful starting point, not a promise that every size and color is immediately available or that a new custom pattern can be produced at the same minimum. Send the style code, chosen color, quantity by size, branding, destination and desired timing. Ask whether logos, labels, hang tags or packaging can be added to that exact style.</p>
  <p>If your brand requires a new flare shape, a particular inseam, pockets or an original waistband, send a tech pack or annotated reference. Approve the first physical sample, revise the measurement table as needed, and retain the final approved sample for inspection and reorders. This makes “flare yoga pants wholesale” a specific, comparable purchase rather than a vague request for a look.</p>
